/*
Problem: Construct String from Binary Tree (LC 606)
Topic: Binary Tree / DFS

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Traverse the tree in preorder:

Root -> Left -> Right

For every node:

• Add its value.

• If a left child exists,
  enclose its string in parentheses.

• If there is no left child but a
  right child exists, add empty
  parentheses "()" to preserve the
  one-to-one tree mapping.

• If a right child exists,
  enclose its string in parentheses.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. If node is NULL,
   return "".

2. Add current node value.

3. Recursively build the left string.

4. If the node has a left child or a
   right child, append:

   "(" + left + ")"

5. Recursively build the right string.

6. If the node has a right child,
   append:

   "(" + right + ")"

7. Return the final string.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

        1
       / \
      2   3
     /
    4

Output:

"1(2(4))(3)"

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

        1
         \
          2

Output:

"1()(2)"

The empty parentheses are necessary
to indicate that node 1 has no left
child.

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Preorder traversal naturally places
the parent before its children.

Parentheses preserve the tree
structure.

The empty "()" is required only when
a right child exists without a left
child; otherwise, the tree structure
would become ambiguous.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Every node is visited once.

Space : O(h)

h = height of tree
(recursion stack)

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Tree DFS (Preorder Traversal)
*/

class Solution {
public:
    string tree2str(TreeNode* root) {

        if (root == NULL)
            return "";

        string s = "";

        // Current node
        s += to_string(root->val);

        // Left subtree
        string left = tree2str(root->left);

        if (root->left || root->right) {
            s += "(" + left + ")";
        }

        // Right subtree
        string right = tree2str(root->right);

        if (root->right) {
            s += "(" + right + ")";
        }

        return s;
    }
};
